  AVPA_Calibration

      ViStatus AVPA_Calibration (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                 ViInt16 elementtoCalibrate,
                                 ViReal64 calibrationLevel,
                                 ViBoolean calibrationCorrection,
                                 ViBoolean frequencyCorrection);

  Purpose

      Specifies the type of calibration required and starts it. Don't forget to
      link the output connector CAL OUT and the input connector

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      elementtoCalibrate

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          specifies which element to calibrate
          
          Valid Range :
          0 - All (Default)
          1 - Total Gain
          2 - Input Attenuator
          3 - IF step Amplifier
          4 - RBW switch
          5 - Logarithmic linearity
          6 - Amplifier Magnitude
          7 - PBW
          
          

      calibrationLevel

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          specifies the level of the output signal of calibration.
          
          Valid Range: -10 dB to -30 dB (Default)
          
          

      calibrationCorrection

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          specifies whether to activate or desactivate the calibration factor
          obtain after the calibration.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_ON - ON
          VI_OFF - OFF

      frequencyCorrection

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          specifies whether to activate or desactivate the frequency
          correction.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_ON - ON (Default)
          VI_OFF - OFF

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Element to Calibrate) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Calibration Level) out of range.
          BFFC0004  Parameter 4 (Calibration Correction) out of range.
          BFFC0005  Parameter 5 (Frequency Correction) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
