  AVPA_configRead

      ViStatus AVPA_configRead (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViBoolean tracetoRead,
                                ViInt16 typeofSearch, ViInt16 traceDataArray[],
                                ViReal64 *sweepTime, ViChar sweepUnit[],
                                ViReal64 *markerPosition, ViReal64 *markerLevel);

  Purpose

      This function performs the following operations:
      1 - returns the trace Data of the chosen trace in an array.
      2 - reads the sweep time : value and unit.
      3 - searches the desired peak and returns its coordinates.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      tracetoRead

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          selects the trace to store in an array.
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON - Trace A (Default)
          VI_OFF - Trace B
          

      typeofSearch

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          selects the peak marker search desired
          
          Valid Range :
          0 - peak search (Default)
          1 - next peak
          2 - next peak left
          3 - next peak right
          4 - min search
          5 - next minimum
          
          

      traceDataArray

          Variable Type       ViInt16[]

          This is the array where the function will write the trace data.
          

      sweepTime

          Variable Type       ViReal64 (passed by reference)

          returns the value of the sweep time value.

      sweepUnit

          Variable Type       ViChar[]

          returns the sweep time unit.
          

      markerPosition

          Variable Type       ViReal64 (passed by reference)

          returns the position of the marker normal ie the position of the
          peak searched.

      markerLevel

          Variable Type       ViReal64 (passed by reference)

          returns the level of the marker normal ie the level of the peak
          searched.
          

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Trace to Read) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Type of Search) out of range.
          BFFC0803  Invalid Response VI_ERROR_INSTR_INTERPRETING_RESPONSE
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
