  AVPA_Copy_Screen

      ViStatus AVPA_Copy_Screen (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViInt16 copyMode);

  Purpose

      This function is used to start a screen copy toward the printer. The
      aspect of the screen copy is selected at the same time.This function
      allows to start a screen copy toward the printer. The aspect of the
      screen copy is selected at the same time.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      copyMode

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Selects the type of print output desired.
          
          Valid Range:
          0 - Gray Scale (A4 size)
          1 - Large Black & White (A4 size)
          2 - Small Black & White (screen reduction)
          
          Default Value:
          1 - Large Black & White

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Copy Mode) out of range.
          
