  AVPA_Read_LimitLineOptions

      ViStatus AVPA_Read_LimitLineOptions (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                           ViBoolean levelAxistoCheck,
                                           ViInt16 *levelAxis,
                                           ViChar levelAxismessage[],
                                           ViReal64 *shiftLevel,
                                           ViReal64 *frequencyTimeShift);

  Purpose

      This function returns the modes (absolute/relative) used along the axis
      and the values of the shift level and the shift time or frequency.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      levelAxistoCheck

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          this binary switch is used to select whether you want to check the
          status of the Level/X-Axis or the status of the Level/Y-Axis
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON : X-Axis
          VI_OFF : Y-Axis (Default)

      levelAxis

          Variable Type       ViInt16 (passed by reference)

          this output variable is used to know whether we use the absolute or
          the relative mode along the X or Y Axis.
          
          Valid Range :
          0 - absolute
          1 - relative
          
          

      levelAxismessage

          Variable Type       ViChar[]

          this output variable is used to know whether we use the absolute or
          the relative mode along the X or Y Axis

      shiftLevel

          Variable Type       ViReal64 (passed by reference)

          returns the value of the shift level always expressed in dB

      frequencyTimeShift

          Variable Type       ViReal64 (passed by reference)

          returns the value of the frequency or time shift according to the
          span value. If span is not null, the unit is Hz, otherwise the unit
          is second.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Level/Axis to Check) out of range.
          BFFC0803  Invalid Response VI_ERROR_INSTR_INTERPRETING_RESPONSE
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
