  AVPA_Read_Multimarkers

      ViStatus AVPA_Read_Multimarkers (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                       ViReal64 multimarkersPositions[],
                                       ViReal64 *markerDeltaPosition,
                                       ViReal64 multimarkersLevels[],
                                       ViReal64 *markerDeltaLevel);

  Purpose

      This function is used to read the positions and levels of the 10
      multimarkers and the position and level of the marker delta.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      multimarkersPositions

          Variable Type       ViReal64[]

          this array contains either the positions of the multimarkers when the
          marker delta is inactive or the differences of position  between the
          multimarkers and the marker delta when this last one is active.
          
          When the Multi Marker x is not active, you read zero.

      markerDeltaPosition

          Variable Type       ViReal64 (passed by reference)

          returns the position of the marker delta when it is active and zero
          otherwise.
          
          

      multimarkersLevels

          Variable Type       ViReal64[]

          this array contains :
          - the levels of the multimarkers when marker delta is inactive.
          - the absolute levels of the multimarkers when the marker delta  is
          active and display mode is set on absolute.
          - the level gaps between the multimarkers and the marker delta when
          it is active and display mode set on relative.
          
          When the Multi Marker x is not active, you read zero.
          
          

      markerDeltaLevel

          Variable Type       ViReal64 (passed by reference)

          returns the level of the marker delta when it is active and zero
          otherwise.
          
          

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0803  Invalid Response VI_ERROR_INSTR_INTERPRETING_RESPONSE
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
