  AVPA_Set_Att

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_Att (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViBoolean typeofControl,
                             ViReal64 inputAttenuationValuedB);

  Purpose

      This function is used to configure the input attenuator. Normal (default)
      position is AUTO. This is also the safest position.
      
      Note : the input attenuation setting is conditioned by the minimum
      attenuation setting: a value smaller than the minimum attenuation cannot
      be set. This limitation is controlled by the analyzer itself.
      

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      typeofControl

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This Binary Switch allows to control the input attenuation manually
          or to let the spectrum analyser choose its value.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_OFF - Manual
          VI_ON - Automatic ( Default)
          
          Note : the other parameter of this function is "Input Attenuation
          Value" which is only valid when "VI_OFF-Manual" is selected by this
          control.
          
          
          

      inputAttenuationValuedB

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          Value that the input attenuation should be set to.
          
          Data Range: 0 to 70 dB
          
          Default Value : 10 dB
          
          Warning: the analyzer will not set input attenuation under the
          minimum attenuation setting. If a value less than the minimum is set
          here the minimum attenuation will be set instead.
          
          Note : the Input Attenuation is always expressed in dB.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Type of Control) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Input Attenuation Value) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
