  AVPA_Set_Freq

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_Freq (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViInt16 frequencyType,
                              ViReal64 frequencyValueHz);

  Purpose

      This function sets the specified frequency (Frequency Type) to the
      specified value (Frequency value).

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      frequencyType

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          The Frequency Type determines which frequency parameter must be set
          between the center frequency and the start or stop frequency.
          
          Valid Range :
          0 - Center (Default)
          1 - Start
          2 - Stop
          
          

      frequencyValueHz

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          The frequency value to be set for either the center, start or stop
          frequency depending on the Frequency Type setting.
          
          Center frequency valid range :
          0 to 3 GHz for the R3263 and R3463
          0 to 8 GHZ for the R3465
          0 to 26.5 GHz for the R3272
          
          Start frequency valid range :
          -200 MHz to 3 GHz for the R3263 and R3463
          -200 MHz to 8 GHZ for the R3465
          -200 MHz to 26.5 GHz for the R3272
          
          Stop frequency valid range :
          0 to 3.2 GHz for the R3263 and R3463
          0 to 8.2 GHZ for the R3465
          0 to 26.7 GHz for the R3272
          
          Default Value: 1 GHz
          
          Note : the frequency is always expressed in Hz

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Frequency Type) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Frequency Value) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
