  AVPA_Set_GatedSweep

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_GatedSweep (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViBoolean gatedSweep,
                                    ViInt16 gateSource, ViBoolean gateSourceSlope,
                                    ViReal64 gatePositionsec, ViReal64 gateWidthsec);

  Purpose

      This function is used to configure and activate or desactivate the Gated
      Sweep Mode

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      gatedSweep

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          Activate or desactivate the Gated Sweep mode.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_OFF - OFF (Default)
          VI_ON - ON
          
          Note: If trigger signal is incorrect the analyzer might then fall
          into an endless wait loop.
          

      gateSource

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Selects the gate source ie the signal used as a trigger for
          positionning the gate.
          
          Data Range:
          0 - IF Signal (Default Value)
          1 - External Gate IN
          2 - External Trigger
          
          Notes :
          (1) IF Signal : Internal IF signal
          (2) External Gate IN : Gate signal connected to the GATE IN
          connector at the rear panel of analyzer
          (3) External Trigger : Pulse TTL signal connected to the
          external trigger connector at the rear panel of the analyzer
          

      gateSourceSlope

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          Selects the polarity of the external trigger signal
          
          Data Range:
          VI_OFF : -Slope
          VI_ON : +Slope (Default)
          
          

      gatePositionsec

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          Gate Position: Time at which the gate should start.
          
          Data Range : 1e-6 to 65e-3 sec
          
          Default Value : 1e-6 sec
          

      gateWidthsec

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          Gate width: size of the gate. Gate starts at Gate Position and ends
          at Gate Position + Gate Width.
          
          Data Range : 2e-6 to 65e-3 sec
          
          Default Value : 5e-3 sec

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Gated Sweep) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Gate Source) out of range.
          BFFC0004  Parameter 4 (Gate Source Slope) out of range.
          BFFC0005  Parameter 5 (Gate Position) out of range.
          BFFC0006  Parameter 6 (Gate Width) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
