  AVPA_Set_LevelCorrection

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_LevelCorrection (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                         ViBoolean levelCorrection,
                                         ViString levelCorrectionFrequencyTable,
                                         ViString levelCorrectionLevelTable);

  Purpose

      This function is used to activate or desactivate the level correction
      function and to set up the table of level correction.
      
      

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      levelCorrection

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          specifies whether the input level correction is active (ON) or
          inactive (OFF).
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_ON - ON
          VI_OFF - OFF (Default)
          
          

      levelCorrectionFrequencyTable

          Variable Type       ViString

          Frequencies table of the correction factor function.
          
          Valid Range : depends on the frequency range studied.
          
          Syntax : "f1,f2,f2,f3"
          
          Note : only the frequency domain is available and the unit is always
          Hz.
          

      levelCorrectionLevelTable

          Variable Type       ViString

          Levels table of the correction factor function.
          
          Valid Range : depends on the level range studied.
          
          Syntax : "l1,l1,l2,l1"
          
          Note : the unit is always the dB.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Level Correction) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
