  AVPA_Set_MarkerDeltaOptions

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_MarkerDeltaOptions (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                            ViBoolean one1DeltaMarker,
                                            ViBoolean markerDeltaFixed,
                                            ViBoolean markerDisplayMode);

  Purpose

      This function is used to set up the options about the Marker Delta.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      one1DeltaMarker

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch is used to activate or desactivate the mode
          "1/Delta Marker".
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON : Active
          VI_OFF : Inactive (Default)
          

      markerDeltaFixed

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch is used to activate or desactivate the mode "Fixed
          Marker Delta".
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON : Active
          VI_OFF : Inactive (Default)
          

      markerDisplayMode

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch is used to select the Marker Display Mode.
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON - Relative (Default)
          VI_OFF - Absolute
          
          Notes :
          (1) if RELATIVE, the analyzer returns the level's gap between the
          markers Normal and Delta.
          (2) if ABSOLUTE, the analyzer returns the absolute level of the
          marker Normal even if the marker Delta is active.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (one (1) / Delta Marker) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Marker Delta Fixed) out of range.
          BFFC0004  Parameter 4 (Marker Display Mode) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
