  AVPA_Set_MeasurementWindow

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_MeasurementWindow (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                           ViBoolean showHideWindow,
                                           ViReal64 windowPosition,
                                           ViReal64 windowWidth);

  Purpose

      This function is used to specify the position and the width of the
      Measurement Window and to activate or desactivate it.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      showHideWindow

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch is used to show or hide the Measurement Window.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_ON - Show
          VI_OFF - Hide (Default)
          
          
          

      windowPosition

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          Specifies the position of the Measurement Window.
          
          Valid Range : depends on the frequency range studied or on the sweep
          time.
          Default Value : 0
          
          Notes :
          (1) When span is not null, window position = position of the window's
          center and unit is Hz.
          (2) When span is null, window position = position of the window's
          left side and unit is second.
          
          

      windowWidth

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          Specifies the width of the Measurement Window.
          
          Valid Range : depends on the frequency range studied or on the sweep
          time.
          Default Value : 0
          
          Notes :
          (1) When span is not null, unit is Hz.
          (2) When span is null, unit is sec.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Show/Hide Window) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
