          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      typeofControl

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          The minimum attenuation can be set either manually (User) or by the
          spectrum analyzer (Automatic).
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_OFF - User
          VI_ON - Automatic (Default)
          
          Note : when "Automatic" is selected the Minimum Input Attenuation is
          set to 10 dB.

      minimumInputAttenuationValue

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          Specifies the minimum input attenuation that can be set when the
          Type of control switch is set to "User".
          
          Data Range: 0 to  70 dB
          
          Default Value:  10 dB   (= value used by the analyzer when the Type
          of Control selector is set to "Automatic").

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Type of Control) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Min. Input Att. Value) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
