  AVPA_Set_PeakSearchOptions

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_PeakSearchOptions (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                           ViBoolean continousPeakSearch,
                                           ViBoolean signalTrack,
                                           ViBoolean coupleToWindow,
                                           ViInt16 peakRange,
                                           ViReal64 peakdeltaYvalue);

  Purpose

      This function is used to determine the value of Peak delta Y, the part of
      the screen where the peak will be searched and activate or desactivate
      the continuous peak search and the signal track.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      continousPeakSearch

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch allows to execute a continuous search of the peak
          or not
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON : Active
          VI_OFF : Inactive (Default)

      signalTrack

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch allows to use the option Signal Track.
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON : Active
          VI_OFF : Inactive (Default)

      coupleToWindow

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch allows to search the peaks only in the measurement
          window.
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_ON : Active
          VI_OFF : Inactive (Default)

      peakRange

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Selects the peak search range.
          
          Valid Range:
          0 - Normal (Default)
          1 - Upper Side
          2 - Lower Side
          
          Notes :
          (1) Normal : searches the next peak among all points of the waveform
          (2) Upper Side : searches the next peak among the trace points
          above the display line
          (3) Lower Side : searches the next peak among the trace points
          below the display line.
          

      peakdeltaYvalue

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          This control is used to set up the value of Peak deltaY.
          
          Valid Range: 0.1 to 10
          Default Value : 1
          

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Continuous Peak Search) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Signal Track) out of range.
          BFFC0004  Parameter 4 (Couple To Window) out of range.
          BFFC0005  Parameter 5 (Peak Range) out of range.
          BFFC0006  Parameter 6 (Peak DeltaY Value) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
