  AVPA_Set_Span

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_Span (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViInt16 spanType,
                              ViReal64 spanValueHz);

  Purpose

      This function lets the user specify the frequency span.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      spanType

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          The Slide "Type of Control" lets the user choose between : Manual,
          Full Span and Zero Span.
          
          Valid Range :
          0 - Manual (Default)
          1 - Full Span
          2 - Zero Span
          
          Notes :
          (1) The other parameter of this function is "Span Value" which is
          only valid when "0-Manual" is selected by this control.
          (2) Full Span : Center Frequency = middle of the frequency range and
          Span = frequency range.
          (3) Zero Span : Span = 0 Hz, Time Domain analysis.
          
          

      spanValueHz

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          This control is used to set up the value of the span when the "Type
          of Control" is on "Manual".
          
          Valid Range :
          0 to 3 GHz for the R3263 and R3463
          0 to 8 GHz for the R3465
          0 to 26.5 GHz for the R3272
          
          Default Value: 100 MHz
          
          Note : The frequency span is always expressed in Hz.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Span Type) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Span Value) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
