  AVPA_Set_SweepMode

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_SweepMode (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViBoolean sweepMode,
                                   ViBoolean windowSweep);

  Purpose

      This function is used to determine whether the sweep is continuous or
      single and to activate or desactivate the Window Sweep.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      sweepMode

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch lets the user choose between continuous or single
          sweep.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_OFF - Single Sweep
          VI_ON - Continuous Sweep (Default)
          
          Notes :
          (1) Continuous Sweep: a new sweep is started whenever a sweep ended.
          Sweep starts now.
          (2) Single Sweep: After one sweep, the sweep stops.

      windowSweep

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          This binary switch lets the user choose whether the sweep is
          performed only within the Measurement Window or not.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_OFF - OFF (Default)
          VI_ON - ON
          
          Note : Set up the window using the function "Set Measurement Window".
          

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Sweep Mode) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Window Sweep) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
