  AVPA_Set_SweepTime

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_SweepTime (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                   ViBoolean typeofControl, ViReal64 sweepTimesec);

  Purpose

      This function is used to set up the Sweep Time.
      
      Automatic sweep time selection can be specified, in which case a sweep
      time is chosen, by the analyzer, depending on the current setting of RBW,
      VBW and SPAN.
      
      SPAN/(RBW * Min(RBW,VBW) * 0.5) = SWEEP TIME. (AUTO mode)

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      typeofControl

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          The Type of Control lets the user choose betwen a manual control or
          an automatic control of the sweep time.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_OFF - Manual
          VI_ON - AUTO (Default)
          
          Note : Automatic control means that the analyzer itself will
          determine the best sweep time depending on the span, RBW and VBW
          settings.
          

      sweepTimesec

          Variable Type       ViReal64

          Value of the sweep time.
          
          Valid Range : 0.05 (Default) to 1000 sec
          
          Note :
          (1) This parameter has no importance if AUTO is selected.
          (2) The sweep Time is always expressed in second
          

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Type of Control) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Sweep Time) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
