  AVPA_Set_TraceAMode

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_TraceAMode (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViInt16 traceAMode,
                                    ViInt16 averageCount, ViBoolean averageMode);

  Purpose

      This function is used to set up the TRACE A mode. Once set up the mode
      becomes active immediately.
      
      Note : if sweep mode is SINGLE, then mode activation will become visible
      at the next sweep!

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      traceAMode

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Selects the mode for the TRACE A.
          
          Valid Range :
          0 - Write (Default)
          1 - View
          2 - Blank
          3 - Max Hold
          4 - Min Hold
          5 - Averaging.
          6 - Clear
          
          

      averageCount

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Sets the number of sweeps over which averaging should be performed.
          
          Data Range : 2 to 999
          
          Default Value : 20
          
          Note : This setting is ignored if the trace A mode is not on
          "Averaging".
          

      averageMode

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          Specifies the average mode.
          
          Valid Range :
          VI_OFF - Single
          VI_ON - Continuous (Default)
          
          Note : This setting is ignored when trace A mode is not on
          "Averaging".
          
          
          Let the following notation be defined:
            n      current averaging count
            N      Averaging count specified (see control Averaging Count)
            Yn     Trace data for nth average
            <Yn>   Averaged data for nth average
            <Yn-1> Averaged data for n-1 th average
            Sigma  Sum of all the data up to the nth point.
          
          Algorithm 1
          [n<=N]  <Yn> = Sigma/n
          
          Algorithm 2
          [N<n]   <Yn> = ((N-1) - <Yn-1>) / N + <Yn> / N
          
          * When Continuous is selected averaging is repeated using algorithm 2
          even after the specified average count has been reached.
          
          * When Single is selected the analyzer will automatically leave the
          averaging mode for View mode, as soon as the specified average count
          has been reached.
          
          
          

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Trace A Mode) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Average Count) out of range.
          BFFC0004  Parameter 4 (Average Mode) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
________________________________________________________________________________

  AVPA_Set_TraceBMode

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_TraceBMode (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViInt16 traceBMode);

  Purpose

      This function is used to set up the mode of the Trace B. Once set up the
      mode becomes active immediately.
      
       Note : Trace B has not the same purpose of Trace A. Trace B does not
      have a Write mode.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      traceBMode

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Selects the mode of the Trace B.
          
          Valid Range:
          0 - B Store
          1 - B View
          2 - B Blank (Default)
          
          Note : B Store means that the spectrum analyser store the Trace A
          into the Trace B.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Trace B Mode) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
________________________________________________________________________________

  AVPA_Set_TraceDetector

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_TraceDetector (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                       ViInt16 detectorMode);

  Purpose

      This function is used to select the Trace Detector Mode that will be used
      to display the data.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      detectorMode

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          This control determines the detector mode that will now be used.
          
          Valid Range:
          0 - Posi-Nega (Default)
          1 - Positive
          2 - Negative
          3 - Sample
          
          Notes :
          (1) Posi-Nega:this is the normal mode.
          (2) Positive:the maximum level measured since the last point is
          assigned to the screen point
          (3) Negative:the minimum level measured since the last point is
          assigned to the screen point
          (4) Sample:the level at the screen point is taken for the screen
          point.

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Detector Mode) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
________________________________________________________________________________

