  AVPA_Set_TriggerMode

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_TriggerMode (ViSession instrumentHandle,
                                     ViInt16 triggerSource,
                                     ViBoolean polarityofEXTERNALTrigger,
                                     ViInt16 levelinforVideoTrigger);

  Purpose

      This function is used to set up the Trigger Mode, the polarity of an
      external trigger and the level for the video trigger.

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      triggerSource

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Selects the trigger source.
          
          Data Range:
          0 - Free run (Default)
          1 - Line
          2 - Video
          3 - External
          
          Notes:
          (1) Free run : no trigger, repeat sweep
          (2) Line : synchronization with AC supply frequency
          (3) Video : Starts the sweep when level of video signal
                               is over the trigger level
          (4) External : synchronization with a TTL signal connected
                               to the "external trigger input" connector
                               at the rear panel of the analyzer
          

      polarityofEXTERNALTrigger

          Variable Type       ViBoolean

          Selects the polarity of the external trigger signal.
          
          Valid Range:
          VI_0FF : -Slope
          VI_ON : +Slope (Default Value)
          
          

      levelinforVideoTrigger

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          Value of the level of the video trigger.
          
          Valid Range : 0 to 100 %
          Default Value : 30 %
          
          Note : this value is expressed in % of the Y axis of the display
          screen.
          

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (Trigger Source) out of range.
          BFFC0003  Parameter 3 (Polarity of Ext. Trigger) out of range.
          BFFC0004  Parameter 4 (Level for Video Trigger) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
________________________________________________________________________________

  AVPA_Set_VBW

      ViStatus AVPA_Set_VBW (ViSession instrumentHandle, ViInt16 VBWSetting);

  Purpose

      This function is used to set up the bandwidth of the video filter.
      
      

  Parameter List

      instrumentHandle

          Variable Type       ViSession

          This control accepts the Instrument Handle returned by the Initialize
          function to select the desired instrument driver session.
          
          Default Value:  None

      VBWSetting

          Variable Type       ViInt16

          This control is used to specify the value of the bandwidth of the
          video filter (VBW).
          
          Valid Range:
          0 - AUTO  (Default)
          1 - 1 Hz
          2 - 3 Hz
          3 - 10 Hz
          4 - 30 Hz
          5 - 100 Hz
          6 - 300 Hz
          7 - 1 kHz
          8 - 3 kHz
          9 - 10 kHz
          10 - 30 kHz
          11 - 100 kHz
          12 - 300 kHz
          13 - 1 MHz
          14 - 3 MHz
          15 - 5 MHz
          
          Notes :
          (1) Automatic VBW can be selected in which case the analyzer will
          automatically choose VBW according to RBW.
          (2) The ratio VBW:RBW can be modified using the "Set RBW/VBW
          Coupling" function.
          (3) For noise averaging, VBW is often chosen 1/10 under RBW (RBW =
          300 kHz -> VBW = 30 kHz)

  Return Value

          This control contains the status code returned by the function call.
          
          Status Codes:
          
          Status    Description
          -------------------------------------------------
                 0  No error (the call was successful).
          
          BFFC0002  Parameter 2 (VBW Setting) out of range.
          
          BFFF0000  Miscellaneous or system error occurred.
          BFFF000E  Invalid session handle.
          BFFF0015  Timeout occurred before operation could complete.
          BFFF0034  Violation of raw write protocol occurred.
          BFFF0035  Violation of raw read protocol occurred.
          BFFF0036  Device reported an output protocol error.
          BFFF0037  Device reported an input protocol error.
          BFFF0038  Bus error occurred during transfer.
          BFFF003A  Invalid setup (attributes are not consistent).
          BFFF005F  No listeners condition was detected.
          BFFF0060  This interface is not the controller in charge.
          BFFF0067  Operation is not supported on this session.
          
